Sky1 firmware publishes the 18-character connection ID
"fch_timer_func_clk". The clkdev allocator rejects it because its
16-byte array also has to hold the terminating NUL.

Raise the storage to 32 bytes, matching the strict CIX CLKT and CLKA
parser bound. Keep the unrelated device-ID limit unchanged.

This retains the vendor behavior with its firmware dependency explicit.
Link: https://github.com/cixtech/cix-linux-main/commit/19f2947303670f2e5734d6a96ffc72a80fd9b942

diff --git a/drivers/clk/clkdev.c b/drivers/clk/clkdev.c
--- a/drivers/clk/clkdev.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clkdev.c
@@ -145,7 +145,7 @@ void clkdev_add_table(struct clk_lookup *cl, size_t num)
 }
 
 #define MAX_DEV_ID	24
-#define MAX_CON_ID	16
+#define MAX_CON_ID	32
 
 struct clk_lookup_alloc {
 	struct clk_lookup cl;
